CORE
negative-part-select-base2.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.v\[7\+:2\] !== 2'b11: PROVED up to bound 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^Invariant check failed
^Reason: index_as_int
--
1800-2017 11.5.1: when the selected range of an indexed part-select
falls partly or wholly outside the vector bounds, the out-of-range bits
read as x (4-state) rather than causing an error.  v[7 +: 2] selects
in-range bit 7 (1) and out-of-range bit 8 (x), so the result is not
2'b11 and the property should be PROVED with EXIT=0.
